                  "The lesson for anyone teaching online is that frequent testing works for memory, but the returns fall off fast. The second quiz added almost nothing and lost half the room. Applying knowledge came from conversation and real work with the lecturer as adviser, not from media that looked sophisticated. So the researchers suggest fewer memory tests, more varied questions, one place for all the quizzes, and a live discussion about every thirty minutes of lecture.",
